==============================================================================
O18 — joint multiplicative ladder  (fit-free; exact counts; projection, not fit)
==============================================================================
  O17 showed a geometric ladder of ratio r samples log x at spacing log(r), so the
  projection Nyquist is pi/log(r): 4.5324 for base 2 and 2.8595 for base 3, both far
  below gamma_1 = 14.134725. Each integer base alone is therefore blind to every zero.
  This script asks whether the bases are blind JOINTLY. The semigroup {2^m 3^n} is
  IRREGULARLY spaced in log x, and irregular sampling is NOT bound by the uniform
  rate. Interpretation of the numbers below is NOT this script's job.

  x0 = 1000   xmax = 150000000   dps = 30   surrogates = 200   seed = 2026
  pi/log2 = 4.532360     pi/log3 = 2.859601

  sieving primes to 150000000...
  8444396 primes, largest = 149999957

